{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:35.581308Z","id":"a25be44a76101761b30631921da1fade2981b01b7a24499ac0e1fbdf27f07b92","body":{"detail":"cargo test, clippy and fmt in scripts/quality_gates.sh run on the root workspace only, so the VFS's tests (crates/clax-worker/vfs/tests) and the wasm32 build of clax-worker never run in a gate. The native tests also cover only the VFS against an in-memory PageStore: DoPageStore (crates/clax-worker/src/store.rs: the upsert/delete SQL, i64 and f64 bindings, transactionSync through Reflect) and the wasm SQLite build (sqlite-wasm-rs 0.5.5 with SQLITE_DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE=-16384 and SQLITE_DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE=8192, versus libsqlite3-sys natively) are exercised only by hand under wrangler dev.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"ff367854fd9e0067856a97495d8e9fdd046761208bd88ef5d9c19f95d00734c7"},"suggested_fix":"Add a lane running cargo test/clippy/fmt in crates/clax-worker, a wasm32 build check, and a scripted wrangler dev --local run of the routes (fill, abort, stats?check=1) across a restart.","summary":"No gate runs clax-worker or clax-do-vfs: the crates are outside the workspace and scripts/quality_gates.sh does not name them","tags":["gates","tests","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:24:31.774226Z","id":"ef9746cdbe0a7102580a35291c8f4f7025c78312848d91f50afde3cb97b54dbf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0bf47593","summary":"Fixed in 0bf47593: lane_worker in scripts/quality_gates.sh runs, in crates/clax-worker, cargo fmt --check, cargo test --workspace, cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings, and node test-wasm.mjs, which runs build.sh, starts wrangler dev --local on free ports with a fresh --persist-to under crates/clax-worker/target/wasm-test/, writes through init, notes, abort, fill, journal and stats?check=1, restarts wrangler and compares notes, blobs, page counts, the blob digest and integrity_check. Evidence: each lane command, run alone on macOS, exits 0 (npm ci 17 s on its first run, fmt 0 s, test 5 s, clippy 1 s, test-wasm.mjs 15 s warm), and test-wasm.mjs ends with {\"ok\":true,...}. The Linux build in CI is unverified: see the concern on crates/clax-worker/build.sh:13:19.","supersedes":"a25be44a76101761b30631921da1fade2981b01b7a24499ac0e1fbdf27f07b92","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"CLA.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T03:59:18.868830Z","id":"af83eaac9e52ac2478b7435ddeced857822d39e56a98b7f41d0c827cb769de01","body":{"detail":"CLA.md (version 1.0) restates the terms of the Apache Software Foundation's Individual Contributor License Agreement for Empathic, Inc., with section 2 naming the right to distribute Contributions under GPL-2.0, AGPL-3.0 and any other terms Empathic chooses. It was drafted without legal review. Open: (1) review by counsel; (2) whether to add a commitment that Empathic will keep distributing Contributions under an OSI-approved license (some CLAs, such as the Harmony Agreements' outbound options, offer one; Apache's and Google's do not); (3) where signed copies are kept (CONTRIBUTING.md says email to alex@empathic.dev, kept by Empathic, unpublished).","kind":"concern","summary":"Have counsel review CLA.md before collecting signatures, and decide whether it promises an open-source outbound license","tags":["status:needs-decision","legal","session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"justfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:33:35.625613Z","id":"42e1d65c3e62b9776e3606fc30363c30d65d435394a2f0d5a06486dd42c7be7b","body":{"detail":"Failure: 'flutter test integration_test -d macos' with more than one *_test.dart file. The first file runs; each later one is built, then fails with 'Error waiting for a debug connection: The log reader stopped unexpectedly, or never started.' and 'Unable to start the app on the device'. Seen 2026-10-13 with locked_daemon_test.dart + full_loop_test.dart (target/flutter-app/i1.log) and with tool_loop_test.dart + full_loop_test.dart (target/flutter-app/i1-multi-v.log), with no other macOS build running. Each file passes in its own invocation (the built Debug app also starts on its own and prints its VM service URL). The cause inside flutter_tools or macOS was not found. apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart now runs tool_loop.dart's test in its own launch, so the integration tests are two files: full_loop_test.dart and locked_daemon_test.dart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":128},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"96540e8f8d84c7b159511b64ed2e76491a9fa247b2cc50b64c0fcc5e0a9d0fda"},"suggested_fix":"Run each file in its own invocation: 'cd apps/clax_app && for f in integration_test/*_test.dart; do flutter test \"$f\" -d macos || exit 1; done', or give the folder a single entry file that calls each scenario.","summary":"just app-integration launches one app per test file, and on macOS every file after the first fails to launch","tags":["integration","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"MODULE.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.328869Z","id":"74b6aeeeaf76b82f813f86b7f67ee1da9f61b9e3acc4bbbe08b46739b14eb4b9","body":{"detail":"rules_flutter (github.com/aran/rules_flutter, 0.0.6, released 2026-10-16) was taken: it fetches Flutter 3.47.7, its engines and every pub package by checksum, compiles kernel and AOT, runs flutter_tester, and builds APKs with rules_android and macOS apps with rules_apple, on Bazel 9. It is alpha (its README: 'the public API may still change'), one maintainer, and needed three patches here (bazel/flutter/rules_flutter.patch) and a composed APK macro (bazel/flutter/android.bzl). Writing the same from scratch was not worth it while it is maintained.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":161},"end":{"line":185},"content_hash":"3e9da6d4ded7f6f517d7abc6d543921a147131562f57756d9e38b5259b5e40e8"},"summary":"Own Starlark rules for Flutter instead of rules_flutter","tags":["revisit:rules_flutter goes a quarter without a release, or a version bump breaks bazel/flutter/","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"justfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.329361Z","id":"c6d27cf4629f0a837c06af20b2dffd2efd222962a089e00a182e007424e5083e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"42e1d65c3e62b9776e3606fc30363c30d65d435394a2f0d5a06486dd42c7be7b","summary":"With Bazel, just app-integration runs each file as its own app and test target (//apps/clax_app:integration_<name>, exclusive), not one flutter test call: on 2026-10-17 integration_locked_daemon and integration_bundle passed in one bazelisk test invocation with integration_full_loop (which failed in its second test, as it does under flutter test too). The native recipe (just app-integration-native) still runs one flutter test per file.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.087090Z","id":"5fbef8bdb5089ab7e2ebdb0ba00c7a56ddee459d6318824139c5007a0710d0a6","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). rmcp is the MCP SDK used by crates/clax-commands and crates/clax-mcp (Cargo.toml: rmcp.workspace); rmcp-macros (Cargo.lock:2185) is its proc-macro. bazel cquery 'deps(//crates/clax-cli:clax_android_arm64)' reaches both, so the APK's libclax.so carries rmcp. The same crates are in main's GPL-2.0-only clax (relicensed in b97323d0d773 without a recorded audit of third-party crates), so the decision is the whole project's. Options: (a) an additional permission in LICENSE for Apache-2.0 libraries; (b) replace rmcp with an MCP implementation under a GPL-2.0-compatible license (MIT or BSD), or Clax's own.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2151},"end":{"line":2160},"content_hash":"1109079ada30e5ed1b5f71aeb0e97e4f40a4286f8125862d0c244d083b7f5154"},"summary":"The app's clax (and main's GPL-2.0-only clax) links rmcp 3.5.0 and rmcp-macros, Apache-2.0 only","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.087182Z","id":"9200d22d888cc4b91885724ab2409c01cedbebd8d89518dcc3d40020c5e18cb1","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). ring is a direct dependency of crates/clax-core (Cargo.toml: ring.workspace) and of rustls, which reqwest uses for TLS; its Cargo.toml declares 'Apache-2.0 AND ISC', so its Apache-2.0 parts bind. It is in the APK's libclax.so and in main's GPL-2.0-only clax alike. Options: (a) an additional permission in LICENSE for Apache-2.0 libraries; (b) move clax-core's use to RustCrypto crates (MIT OR Apache-2.0) and rustls to a RustCrypto provider; aws-lc-rs is no better (Apache-2.0 AND ISC, OpenSSL).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2137},"end":{"line":2142},"content_hash":"743516077ba59fac4071bdab0ed4e015cc351a70125edde9183104e8efbc12ab"},"summary":"The app's clax (and main's) links ring 0.17.14, licensed Apache-2.0 AND ISC, under GPL-2.0-only","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.087268Z","id":"2e6e83c78b053e2730e47956d1d6b3039c9b7b1d2c48591dc8ada2550b09e681","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). sync_wrapper is a dependency of axum, axum-core, tower and reqwest (Cargo.lock), not of Clax's own code, and is in the APK's libclax.so and main's GPL-2.0-only clax alike. Options: (a) an additional permission in LICENSE for Apache-2.0 libraries (practical: axum, tower and reqwest all need it); (b) ask upstream to dual-license it MIT OR Apache-2.0, as most of the ecosystem is.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2635},"end":{"line":2640},"content_hash":"0cdb210e1d4931cbcc8570105a759bb82f731749807f367f3fcc855047791479"},"summary":"The app's clax (and main's) links sync_wrapper 1.0.2, Apache-2.0 only, through axum, tower and reqwest","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"MODULE.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:39:08.877840Z","id":"aa6f6613eac5a56b2e2a97cf0a6ec009de378ab7011e438c0c9bd2d2022d6e4f","body":{"detail":"@androidsdk unpacks every row of its archives whenever it is fetched (every APK build), and bazel/android/rules_android.patch fails for a directory with no row for the host OS, so the rows would also need a Linux emulator. The system image unpacks to 4.4 GB. As @android_emulator and @android_system_image only //apps/clax_app:integration_android_* (and scripts/app-android-emulator.sh) fetch them.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":288},"end":{"line":313},"content_hash":"a717eb3cb9959674168ff0efdf1b26aa92eda0f045d3d780c157ad5b5f16cc61"},"summary":"The Android emulator and system image are http_archives of their own, not rows of android_sdk.configure's archives","tags":["revisit:a target other than the manual Android integration tests needs the emulator or the system image","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.171109Z","id":"24c87cd22fb62f531dbbaa0ebf7540913795c3b0c9ec7827378846deae14fd9f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5fbef8bdb5089ab7e2ebdb0ba00c7a56ddee459d6318824139c5007a0710d0a6","summary":"The app no longer ships //crates/clax-cli:clax_android_*: it ships the embedded core, and clax-embed still reaches rmcp and rmcp-macros through clax-server and clax-mcp (cargo metadata --offline: clax-embed's normal dependency closure includes rmcp and rmcp-macros), so this stands for the APK's, the Mac app's and the iOS app's core.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"justfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:57.162211Z","id":"d869139a84a869b1c83f024929dcaa01e42e5eaf552bf3605971c195b423b0c1","body":{"detail":"The recipe runs `cargo package ... --target-dir ../pack`, which writes target/crate-package/pack/package/clax-<version>.crate and never removes older ones; scripts/crate-package.py rewrites only target/crate-package/clax. After a version bump (scripts/bump-version.sh) the next run's `tar -xzf target/crate-package/pack/package/clax-*.crate -C ...` expands to `tar -xzf clax-0.4.0.crate clax-0.5.0.crate -C ...`: tar takes the second file as a member name to extract from the first, fails with \"Not found in archive\", and the recipe stops (or, if the order differs, unpacks the old version). The `cd target/crate-package/unpacked/clax-*` on line 191 has the same shape but is safe only because line 188 recreates that directory.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":184},"end":{"line":191},"content_hash":"db81abc8d9ec00000db4fcdd4af537e51aa5d492a1067abad51ebc8afda21687"},"suggested_fix":"Remove target/crate-package/pack/package before `cargo package` (add it to line 188's rm -rf), or name the archive exactly from the version: `tar -xzf target/crate-package/pack/package/clax-$(scripts/check-version.sh --print).crate`.","summary":"`just crate-package` fails once target/crate-package/pack holds a .crate of an earlier version: the tar glob expands to two archives","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"justfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:57.162249Z","id":"a9247708da95cbe8e2cb76913b228bd830974ad73e018ec7dd3707e9919d441f","body":{"detail":"`test`, `test-native`, `build`, `web`, `web-test`, `pi-test`, `web-e2e`, `lint`, `check`, `ci`, `perf`, `check-wasm` and `serve` (justfile lines 33-34, 68-69, 97-166) use `{{ARGS}}`, which just substitutes as raw text before bash parses the line. A common nextest filter, `just test-native -E 'test(foo)'`, becomes `./scripts/run.sh test -E test(foo)` and bash fails with a syntax error at `(`; `just test -- --test_arg='a b'` splits into two words; a `;` or `$(...)` in an argument runs as shell. `dev`, `watch`, `hosted-demo` and `hosted-deploy` already use `[positional-arguments]` with \"$@\", which passes each argument intact (https://just.systems/man/en/recipe-parameters.html, positional arguments).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":142},"content_hash":"a07552e0d8dfd479a629861746601d6a7ada52eb271fcf79997850cdf0ab859d"},"suggested_fix":"Mark every recipe that forwards *ARGS/*GATES with `[positional-arguments]` and pass \"$@\" (e.g. `./scripts/run.sh test \"$@\"`), as dev and watch do; or set `set positional-arguments` once at the top of the justfile.","summary":"Recipes that pass `{{ARGS}}` paste the arguments into the shell line unquoted, so an argument with spaces or shell syntax breaks or is re-parsed","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"justfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:47.489157Z","id":"718a6b8edb821548bb1f350b77490ce86becb8b005bcef94ab789d3e5e7dce4d","body":{"detail":"justfile:1 `set shell := [\"bash\", \"-cu\"]`, no `set positional-arguments`; e.g. `test-native *ARGS:` runs `CLAX_BUILD=native ./scripts/run.sh test {{ARGS}}` (same shape for test, build, web, web-test, web-e2e, pi-test, check, ci, perf, serve, check-wasm). just substitutes text before bash parses, so `just test-native -E 'test(foo)'` yields `... test -E test(foo)`, a bash syntax error. `[positional-arguments]` appears only at justfile:11, 16, 194, 199.","kind":"comment","references":"a9247708da95cbe8e2cb76913b228bd830974ad73e018ec7dd3707e9919d441f","summary":"confirmed: {{ARGS}} is pasted unquoted into bash lines","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"justfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:47.489482Z","id":"e3a02c1db637cfc7c5355479864b0af30cb5cecc1721959ea4cb97ea8a183086","body":{"detail":"justfile crate-package recipe: `cargo package ... --target-dir ../pack`, then `rm -rf target/crate-package/unpacked` only, then `tar -xzf target/crate-package/pack/package/clax-*.crate -C ...`. scripts/crate-package.py:277-279 rmtree's only OUT (target/crate-package/clax); nothing removes pack/package, so after scripts/bump-version.sh the glob expands to two files and tar treats the second as a member name.","kind":"comment","references":"d869139a84a869b1c83f024929dcaa01e42e5eaf552bf3605971c195b423b0c1","summary":"confirmed: stale .crate files in target/crate-package/pack/package make the tar glob match two archives","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"justfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:57:11.130944Z","id":"895a66ae8027dac23517116ac107034d02c611a92c397634fa7b03fe15826e07","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4c60a0151","summary":"Fixed: justfile sets positional-arguments and forwards \"$@\"; scripts/test-justfile.sh passes args with spaces and shell syntax intact through 20 recipes (failed before).","supersedes":"a9247708da95cbe8e2cb76913b228bd830974ad73e018ec7dd3707e9919d441f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"justfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:57:11.451983Z","id":"66104190ddc321aa0e6ebb4646971517560988c2f6b15943056fbfa138a1f04c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5f18d8f84","summary":"Fixed: crate-package removes target/crate-package/pack/package before cargo package; just --dry-run crate-package shows the step.","supersedes":"d869139a84a869b1c83f024929dcaa01e42e5eaf552bf3605971c195b423b0c1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".bazelrc","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:15:04.896984Z","id":"b283b22d0b79f97d77c8e5e74ed3d602e4efb4d87d0963555a57499794292517","body":{"detail":"Since /Applications/Xcode.app (27.1, 27A9275) was selected on 2026-10-23, apple_support's toolchain sets XCODE_VERSION_OVERRIDE=27.1.0.27A9275 and links with -target arm64-apple-macosx27.0. Proc-macro dylibs it builds (zerofrom_derive, serde_derive, thiserror_impl in darwin_arm64-opt-exec) carry LC_BUILD_VERSION minos 27.0 and dyld refuses them: python3 -c \"import ctypes; ctypes.CDLL('<.dylib>')\" fails 'mis-aligned LINKEDIT string pool', and rustc reports E0463 can't find crate. Copies built before then carry minos 11.0 and load. Those dylibs reached the shared disk cache under the same action keys, so every worktree's Rust build failed. A git-ignored user.bazelrc with build --macos_minimum_os=11.0 --host_macos_minimum_os=11.0 builds and tests pass; the repository sets no macOS minimum itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"2ce6ac66bb8ddbdd60b5f0b3d5bc184ceb7acabd551b6ab55d1add37aeb94437"},"suggested_fix":"Pin --macos_minimum_os and --host_macos_minimum_os in .bazelrc (the deployment target the app ships for), so the link target no longer follows whichever Xcode is selected.","summary":"With Xcode 27.1 selected, Bazel links macOS dylibs with minos 27.0, which dyld refuses (mis-aligned LINKEDIT string pool), so exec-config proc macros fail to load","tags":["bazel","macos","build","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"MODULE.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T20:42:54.398436Z","id":"183d613cd0d82085ab1de817c7ca05d7006f3e38918734356230fce446d80941","body":{"detail":"rustc's strip on Apple targets runs rust-objcopy after the link; it writes the 4-byte indirect symbol table right after the symbol table and the string table right after that, with no padding, so an odd count of indirect symbols leaves stroff 4-byte aligned (libzerofrom_derive in the exec configuration: indirectsymoff 1542968, nindirectsyms 117, stroff 1543436). macOS 27's dyld refuses such a library ('mis-aligned LINKEDIT string pool'). Apple's strip -S on the same input keeps stroff 8-aligned and loads. Letting ld64 omit the debug map (-Clink-arg=-Wl,-S with strip none) would keep the strip, but rules_rust has no per-compilation-mode rustc flag to scope it to opt, and with debuginfo=0 the strip removes only the standard library's debug map: 69 KB of the 56 MB libclax_embed.dylib (Apple strip -S, measured). @rules_rust//util/process_wrapper still passes its own -Cstrip=symbols and is misaligned; it is an executable, which dyld still runs.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":74},"content_hash":"21d03e7d98c9c2fabad83a889cc14ed51e938da9963a4020f439b29793a9024e"},"summary":"Strip opt builds in Apple's linker (-Wl,-S) instead of not stripping","tags":["revisit:a Rust release whose rust-objcopy keeps the Mach-O string table 8-byte aligned, or dyld starts refusing misaligned executables","session:claude-code:a63eca05-dc63-499b-9f6d-066bae1fb314"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"MODULE.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T20:42:54.398574Z","id":"f3000b89f36af624ade1ad339730170cb4b62307cf5316c632ffb6dad059ad71","body":{"detail":"rules_rust 0.74.0 (and main as of 2026-10-23) passes rust.toolchain's strip_level unchanged from rust_register_toolchains (rust/private/repositories.bzl:191) to rust_repository_set, which looks it up by target triple (repositories.bzl:1091) and so finds nothing: the setting is dropped and every toolchain keeps strip_level opt=debuginfo. opt_level is converted per triple two lines above; the patch does the same for strip_level. Spelling the setting as one rust.repository_set per triple would avoid the patch but repeat the toolchain's configuration per triple.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":11},"content_hash":"2388af5a4dc11b88a87600697c5ea34de71a0566d8aa31f5981bd55af6c9c357"},"summary":"Carry bazel/rules_rust.patch rather than per-triple rust.repository_set tags","tags":["revisit:a rules_rust release that converts strip_level per triple in rust_register_toolchains; then drop the override and bazel/rules_rust.patch","session:claude-code:a63eca05-dc63-499b-9f6d-066bae1fb314"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"MODULE.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T20:42:54.398651Z","id":"979627f45fc6c0106f0ee57e9c5219d30b2b83cafaaea7af79c8b8e90211baf2","body":{"detail":"rules_python's explicit_init_py applies only to the module that declares it (rules_python python/extensions/config.bzl:69-72), so the root module cannot set it for rules_apple. The global flag would change every external module's Python targets, not only rules_apple's. All 15 rules_apple py_binary targets that warned were built and run with the patch (each reached its own argument handling; none raised ImportError): they import tools.* as namespace packages, and rules_apple 5.2.0 has no __init__.py files.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":217},"end":{"line":225},"content_hash":"12336f7ad0c8cdbff754dcea78f03c85555cece037856dd933ddec883691f2b2"},"summary":"Patch rules_apple's MODULE.bazel rather than set --incompatible_default_to_explicit_init_py","tags":["revisit:a rules_apple release whose MODULE.bazel declares explicit_init_py; then drop the override and bazel/apple/rules_apple.patch","session:claude-code:a63eca05-dc63-499b-9f6d-066bae1fb314"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T20:42:54.398723Z","id":"508a98db694affaca22bab10ae63bdf3cc06ad85e38ded4a64a3f1b21bb28e50","body":{"detail":"Cargo strips debug information by default in a profile that requests none (release, and build-override for proc macros and build scripts), and rustc on Apple targets strips with rust-objcopy, whose output macOS 27's dyld can refuse ('mis-aligned LINKEDIT string pool'); see the strip_level comment in MODULE.bazel:63-74. Bazel no longer strips, but cargo build --release (scripts/run.sh:285, scripts/quality_gates.sh:162, scripts/build-app-clax.sh:62) has not been run on macOS 27 to confirm.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"52fd4af75cf5b57962f5fa2fb5fdfd4e287bd490c9676c873227e7935c57e859"},"suggested_fix":"Run a -native release build on macOS 27; if it fails the same way, add [profile.release] strip = \"none\" with a comment pointing at MODULE.bazel's strip_level.","summary":"Native release builds on macOS 27 likely fail to load their own proc macros","tags":["session:claude-code:a63eca05-dc63-499b-9f6d-066bae1fb314"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:09.585714Z","id":"a5aff0445ca60c6275c65f26f47c3119cf398d643a596e197b8ff45057de85fb","body":{"detail":"Cargo strips debug information by default in a profile that requests none (release, and build-override for proc macros and build scripts), and rustc on Apple targets strips with rust-objcopy, whose output macOS 27's dyld can refuse ('mis-aligned LINKEDIT string pool'); see the strip_level comment in MODULE.bazel:63-74. Bazel no longer strips, but cargo build --release (scripts/run.sh:285, scripts/quality_gates.sh:162, scripts/build-app-clax.sh:62) has not been run on macOS 27 to confirm.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from the record 508a98db (mailto:alex@kesling.co, session:claude-code:a63eca05-dc63-499b-9f6d-066bae1fb314) onto the lines it concerns, which moved when crates/clax-worker joined the root workspace and Bazel's build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":124},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"52fd4af75cf5b57962f5fa2fb5fdfd4e287bd490c9676c873227e7935c57e859"},"suggested_fix":"Run a -native release build on macOS 27; if it fails the same way, add [profile.release] strip = \"none\" with a comment pointing at MODULE.bazel's strip_level.","summary":"Native release builds on macOS 27 likely fail to load their own proc macros","supersedes":"508a98db694affaca22bab10ae63bdf3cc06ad85e38ded4a64a3f1b21bb28e50","tags":["session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"MODULE.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:09.695471Z","id":"054d4ce08325153c78875358b6ff6c9a09e8b34489dcc428d62a37d294aeaf47","body":{"detail":"rustc's strip on Apple targets runs rust-objcopy after the link; it writes the 4-byte indirect symbol table right after the symbol table and the string table right after that, with no padding, so an odd count of indirect symbols leaves stroff 4-byte aligned (libzerofrom_derive in the exec configuration: indirectsymoff 1542968, nindirectsyms 117, stroff 1543436). macOS 27's dyld refuses such a library ('mis-aligned LINKEDIT string pool'). Apple's strip -S on the same input keeps stroff 8-aligned and loads. Letting ld64 omit the debug map (-Clink-arg=-Wl,-S with strip none) would keep the strip, but rules_rust has no per-compilation-mode rustc flag to scope it to opt, and with debuginfo=0 the strip removes only the standard library's debug map: 69 KB of the 56 MB libclax_embed.dylib (Apple strip -S, measured). @rules_rust//util/process_wrapper still passes its own -Cstrip=symbols and is misaligned; it is an executable, which dyld still runs.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from the record 183d613c (mailto:alex@kesling.co, session:claude-code:a63eca05-dc63-499b-9f6d-066bae1fb314) onto the lines it concerns, which moved when crates/clax-worker joined the root workspace and Bazel's build.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"21d03e7d98c9c2fabad83a889cc14ed51e938da9963a4020f439b29793a9024e"},"summary":"Strip opt builds in Apple's linker (-Wl,-S) instead of not stripping","supersedes":"183d613cd0d82085ab1de817c7ca05d7006f3e38918734356230fce446d80941","tags":["revisit:a Rust release whose rust-objcopy keeps the Mach-O string table 8-byte aligned, or dyld starts refusing misaligned executables","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"MODULE.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:09.802091Z","id":"4b2714e8ff2bd3b1663862f7bb9efc9ca00b7a83832c104c1246eeb33b0a95e9","body":{"detail":"rules_python's explicit_init_py applies only to the module that declares it (rules_python python/extensions/config.bzl:69-72), so the root module cannot set it for rules_apple. The global flag would change every external module's Python targets, not only rules_apple's. All 15 rules_apple py_binary targets that warned were built and run with the patch (each reached its own argument handling; none raised ImportError): they import tools.* as namespace packages, and rules_apple 5.2.0 has no __init__.py files.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from the record 979627f4 (mailto:alex@kesling.co, session:claude-code:a63eca05-dc63-499b-9f6d-066bae1fb314) onto the lines it concerns, which moved when crates/clax-worker joined the root workspace and Bazel's build.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":271},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"12336f7ad0c8cdbff754dcea78f03c85555cece037856dd933ddec883691f2b2"},"summary":"Patch rules_apple's MODULE.bazel rather than set --incompatible_default_to_explicit_init_py","supersedes":"979627f45fc6c0106f0ee57e9c5219d30b2b83cafaaea7af79c8b8e90211baf2","tags":["revisit:a rules_apple release whose MODULE.bazel declares explicit_init_py; then drop the override and bazel/apple/rules_apple.patch","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:30:57.475586Z","id":"beabb2f48ac940556bdcfda6d8853b703e1ef4a7b216b1f79426df17ba9bc33a","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). ring is a direct dependency of crates/clax-core (Cargo.toml: ring.workspace) and of rustls, which reqwest uses for TLS; its Cargo.toml declares 'Apache-2.0 AND ISC', so its Apache-2.0 parts bind. It is in the APK's libclax.so and in main's GPL-2.0-only clax alike. Options: (a) an additional permission in LICENSE for Apache-2.0 libraries; (b) move clax-core's use to RustCrypto crates (MIT OR Apache-2.0) and rustls to a RustCrypto provider; aws-lc-rs is no better (Apache-2.0 AND ISC, OpenSSL).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2890},"end":{"line":2895},"content_hash":"743516077ba59fac4071bdab0ed4e015cc351a70125edde9183104e8efbc12ab"},"summary":"The app's clax (and main's) links ring 0.17.14, licensed Apache-2.0 AND ISC, under GPL-2.0-only","supersedes":"9200d22d888cc4b91885724ab2409c01cedbebd8d89518dcc3d40020c5e18cb1","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:30:57.563984Z","id":"c005ac9d06c73cf07eebdd065a3f9fc8271961f50a825243d6356219dadb3f5d","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). rmcp is the MCP SDK used by crates/clax-commands and crates/clax-mcp (Cargo.toml: rmcp.workspace); rmcp-macros (Cargo.lock:2185) is its proc-macro. bazel cquery 'deps(//crates/clax-cli:clax_android_arm64)' reaches both, so the APK's libclax.so carries rmcp. The same crates are in main's GPL-2.0-only clax (relicensed in b97323d0d773 without a recorded audit of third-party crates), so the decision is the whole project's. Options: (a) an additional permission in LICENSE for Apache-2.0 libraries; (b) replace rmcp with an MCP implementation under a GPL-2.0-compatible license (MIT or BSD), or Clax's own.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2904},"end":{"line":2913},"content_hash":"1109079ada30e5ed1b5f71aeb0e97e4f40a4286f8125862d0c244d083b7f5154"},"summary":"The app's clax (and main's GPL-2.0-only clax) links rmcp 3.5.0 and rmcp-macros, Apache-2.0 only","supersedes":"5fbef8bdb5089ab7e2ebdb0ba00c7a56ddee459d6318824139c5007a0710d0a6","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:30:57.654804Z","id":"2553acb2fe83c23013f3c586f4c8a59ee2bf88c9af29ca00c7e8d557a3f88db9","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). sync_wrapper is a dependency of axum, axum-core, tower and reqwest (Cargo.lock), not of Clax's own code, and is in the APK's libclax.so and main's GPL-2.0-only clax alike. Options: (a) an additional permission in LICENSE for Apache-2.0 libraries (practical: axum, tower and reqwest all need it); (b) ask upstream to dual-license it MIT OR Apache-2.0, as most of the ecosystem is.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3486},"end":{"line":3491},"content_hash":"0cdb210e1d4931cbcc8570105a759bb82f731749807f367f3fcc855047791479"},"summary":"The app's clax (and main's) links sync_wrapper 1.0.2, Apache-2.0 only, through axum, tower and reqwest","supersedes":"2e6e83c78b053e2730e47956d1d6b3039c9b7b1d2c48591dc8ada2550b09e681","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:30:57.744306Z","id":"08139e355e73003ce70560785003b691d44b13b103c93087b445ff142e3f6fee","body":{"detail":"Cargo strips debug information by default in a profile that requests none (release, and build-override for proc macros and build scripts), and rustc on Apple targets strips with rust-objcopy, whose output macOS 27's dyld can refuse ('mis-aligned LINKEDIT string pool'); see the strip_level comment in MODULE.bazel:63-74. Bazel no longer strips, but cargo build --release (scripts/run.sh:285, scripts/quality_gates.sh:162, scripts/build-app-clax.sh:62) has not been run on macOS 27 to confirm.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from the record 508a98db (mailto:alex@kesling.co, session:claude-code:a63eca05-dc63-499b-9f6d-066bae1fb314) onto the lines it concerns, which moved when crates/clax-worker joined the root workspace and Bazel's build.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"52fd4af75cf5b57962f5fa2fb5fdfd4e287bd490c9676c873227e7935c57e859"},"suggested_fix":"Run a -native release build on macOS 27; if it fails the same way, add [profile.release] strip = \"none\" with a comment pointing at MODULE.bazel's strip_level.","summary":"Native release builds on macOS 27 likely fail to load their own proc macros","supersedes":"a5aff0445ca60c6275c65f26f47c3119cf398d643a596e197b8ff45057de85fb","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"MODULE.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:30:57.836928Z","id":"dc3212ebe947c96f5636aed5ea2f557234dde6dbdc541ac7263b1194715d52a8","body":{"detail":"@androidsdk unpacks every row of its archives whenever it is fetched (every APK build), and bazel/android/rules_android.patch fails for a directory with no row for the host OS, so the rows would also need a Linux emulator. The system image unpacks to 4.4 GB. As @android_emulator and @android_system_image only //apps/clax_app:integration_android_* (and scripts/app-android-emulator.sh) fetch them.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":371},"end":{"line":396},"content_hash":"a717eb3cb9959674168ff0efdf1b26aa92eda0f045d3d780c157ad5b5f16cc61"},"summary":"The Android emulator and system image are http_archives of their own, not rows of android_sdk.configure's archives","supersedes":"aa6f6613eac5a56b2e2a97cf0a6ec009de378ab7011e438c0c9bd2d2022d6e4f","tags":["revisit:a target other than the manual Android integration tests needs the emulator or the system image","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"MODULE.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:40.773350Z","id":"84d43502d525af3539ceb5bb4bdab6917b08e0315a2436208edbfe6f0d866d53","body":{"detail":"rules_flutter (github.com/aran/rules_flutter, 0.0.6, released 2026-10-16) was taken: it fetches Flutter 3.47.7, its engines and every pub package by checksum, compiles kernel and AOT, runs flutter_tester, and builds APKs with rules_android and macOS apps with rules_apple, on Bazel 9. It is alpha (its README: 'the public API may still change'), one maintainer, and needed three patches here (bazel/flutter/rules_flutter.patch) and a composed APK macro (bazel/flutter/android.bzl). Writing the same from scratch was not worth it while it is maintained.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":241},"end":{"line":266},"content_hash":"38a779b4d5d5b3327facb15ac010dc228cfe9633c29ecfc6d5ba6825850045f9"},"summary":"Own Starlark rules for Flutter instead of rules_flutter","supersedes":"74b6aeeeaf76b82f813f86b7f67ee1da9f61b9e3acc4bbbe08b46739b14eb4b9","tags":["revisit:rules_flutter goes a quarter without a release, or a version bump breaks bazel/flutter/","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
